RECORD = HEAD EVERYROUTEDVALUEPASSESASDATAANDTHEFRAMEHOLDS READBYVALUEINSTEADEXACTLYTHEFOURSEPARATORBYTESBREAKIT ASTEPATAHELDPOSITIONBREAKSTHEFRAME THEAGENTSORDERDOESNOTCHANGETHEUNITSTHESAMEAGENTWALKEDBACKRESTORESTHEM ASTALEEXCHANGEDOESNOTLAND .

HEAD =
  "// i178.ts — I-178: the frame is held by position; the agents XOR the routed values into the units"
  "//"
  "// The author, 2026-10-12: ""the connecting rule is the allocated raw buffer,"
  "// because entropy degradation is a signal""; the step ""should be xored by user"
  "// agent""; ""all the data is static indices, we are considering the routing; the"
  "// values come from the proxy and the reflect of the user literals from their"
  "// proof tree""; the static indices are ""positions to hold to keep the same frame"
  "// in view or same window""; and the frame is ""Windows and document so fs gs rs"
  "// us can explain it"": the four separators FS 0x1C, GS 0x1D, RS 0x1E, US 0x1F"
  "// (BOOT0, BOOT1, SECURE, USER in the clock notes), file over group over record"
  "// over unit. And: ""the Catch-22 is: all change is outside the system""."
  "//"
  "// So a separator is a separator by its place, not its value: the frame is a"
  "// fixed set of positions, each holding its separator, and the units between"
  "// them carry whatever is routed in, 0x1C-0x1F included, with nothing escaped."
  "// A step is Atomics.compareExchange(state, i, b, b ^ u) by an agent carrying"
  "// the routed byte u, at the static indices 59, 63, 127. The signal is whether"
  "// the frame holds: every held position still shows its separator. The frame"
  "// is the system, and every change lands outside it, in the units."
  "import assert from ""node:assert"";"
  "const SIZE = 256;"
  "const INDICES = [59, 63, 127];"
  "const SEPARATORS = [0x1C, 0x1D, 0x1E, 0x1F]; // FS GS RS US"
  "type Frame = Map<number, number>; // position -> the separator held there"
  "/** One step: the agent reads the byte, then exchanges it for byte ^ agent if it is still what it read. */"
  "function step(state: Uint8Array, index: number, agent: number): boolean {"
  "  const expected = Atomics.load(state, index);"
  "  return Atomics.compareExchange(state, index, expected, expected ^ agent) === expected;"
  "}"
  "/** The raw buffer as allocated, with the frame's separators at their places. */"
  "function document(frame: Frame): Uint8Array {"
  "  const state = new Uint8Array(new SharedArrayBuffer(SIZE));"
  "  for (const [p, sep] of frame) state[p] = sep;"
  "  return state;"
  "}"
  "/** Read by place: the frame holds if every held position shows its separator. */"
  "const holds = (state: Uint8Array, frame: Frame) => [...frame].every(([p, sep]) => state[p] === sep);"
  "/** Read by value, for contrast: where the separators appear, wherever they are. */"
  "const separatorsByValue = (state: Uint8Array) => [...state.keys()].filter((p) => SEPARATORS.includes(state[p]!));"
  "// Frames: fixed places for the four separators, away from the static indices."
  "// They come from a fixed generator, so every run checks the same 64 frames."
  "let seed = 0x4242;"
  "const next = () => (seed = (seed * 1103515245 + 12345) & 0x7FFFFFFF);"
  "const frames: Frame[] = [];"
  "while (frames.length < 64) {"
  "  const frame: Frame = new Map();"
  "  for (const sep of SEPARATORS) {"
  "    let p: number;"
  "    do p = next() % SIZE; while (frame.has(p) || INDICES.includes(p));"
  "    frame.set(p, sep);"
  "  }"
  "  frames.push(frame);"
  "}"
  .

EVERYROUTEDVALUEPASSESASDATAANDTHEFRAMEHOLDS =
  "// ── 1. Every routed value passes as data, and the frame holds ─"
  "// Whatever the proxy or the proof tree routes in is some byte; all 256 are tried."
  "let valueReadBreaks = 0;"
  "for (const frame of frames) {"
  "  const broke: number[] = [];"
  "  const held = [...frame.keys()].sort((a, b) => a - b);"
  "  for (let u = 0; u < 256; u++) {"
  "    const state = document(frame);"
  "    for (const i of INDICES) assert.ok(step(state, i, u), `the step at ${i} lands`);"
  "    const changed = [...state.keys()].filter((p) => state[p] !== (frame.get(p) ?? 0));"
  "    assert.ok(changed.every((p) => INDICES.includes(p) && !frame.has(p)), `routing ${u}: all change is outside the system, in the units`);"
  "    assert.ok(holds(state, frame), `routing ${u} keeps the frame in view`);"
  "    for (const i of INDICES) assert.strictEqual(state[i], u, `the unit at ${i} carries ${u}, as routed`);"
  "    if (separatorsByValue(state).join() !== held.join()) broke.push(u);"
  "  }"
  "  assert.deepStrictEqual(broke, SEPARATORS, ""read by value, exactly the routed values 0x1C-0x1F break this frame"");"
  "  valueReadBreaks += broke.length;"
  "}"
  .

READBYVALUEINSTEADEXACTLYTHEFOURSEPARATORBYTESBREAKIT =
  "// ── 2. Read by value instead, exactly the four separator bytes break it ─"
  "assert.strictEqual(valueReadBreaks, frames.length * SEPARATORS.length, ""4 in each of the 64 frames; read by place, none"");"
  .

ASTEPATAHELDPOSITIONBREAKSTHEFRAME =
  "// ── 3. A step at a held position breaks the frame ───────────"
  "for (const frame of frames) {"
  "  const [p] = frame.keys();"
  "  for (let u = 1; u < 256; u++) {"
  "    const state = document(frame);"
  "    step(state, p!, u);"
  "    assert.ok(!holds(state, frame), `a step of ${u} at the held position ${p} breaks the frame`);"
  "  }"
  "  const state = document(frame);"
  "  step(state, p!, 0);"
  "  assert.ok(holds(state, frame), ""an agent carrying 0 there leaves it held"");"
  "}"
  .

THEAGENTSORDERDOESNOTCHANGETHEUNITSTHESAMEAGENTWALKEDBACKRESTORESTHEM =
  "// ── 4. The agents' order does not change the units; the same agent walked back restores them ─"
  "const frame = frames[0]!;"
  "const routed = [0x55, 0x1D, 0xAA];"
  "const finals = [[0, 1, 2], [2, 0, 1], [1, 2, 0]].map((order) => {"
  "  const state = document(frame);"
  "  for (const k of order) for (const i of INDICES) step(state, i, routed[k]!);"
  "  return INDICES.map((i) => state[i]);"
  "});"
  "const all = 0x55 ^ 0x1D ^ 0xAA;"
  "for (const f of finals) assert.deepStrictEqual(f, [all, all, all], ""each unit is the XOR of what was routed, in any order"");"
  "const state = document(frame);"
  "for (const i of INDICES) step(state, i, 0x1D);"
  "for (const i of [...INDICES].reverse()) step(state, i, 0x1D);"
  "assert.deepStrictEqual(state, document(frame), ""the same agent walked back restores the document"");"
  .

ASTALEEXCHANGEDOESNOTLAND =
  "// ── 5. A stale exchange does not land ───────────────────────"
  "const s = document(frame);"
  "const read = Atomics.load(s, 59);"
  "step(s, 59, 0xAA);"
  "assert.strictEqual(Atomics.compareExchange(s, 59, read, read ^ 0x55), 0xAA, ""a stale exchange returns what is there, and does not land"");"
  "console.log(""I-178: the frame is held by position; the agents XOR the routed values into the units — passed"");"
  "console.log(`  ${frames.length} frames x 256 routed values: the frame held every time, read by place`);"
  "console.log(`  every change landed in the units, outside the frame: all change is outside the system`);"
  "console.log(`  read by value, it broke ${valueReadBreaks} times: the 4 separator bytes in each frame`);"
  .
